\section{Conclusions}\label{sec:conclusion}
We have obtained a common energy-constrained adaptive weak converse for
thermal-loss, noisy amplifier, and additive-noise Gaussian channels.
The input-energy dependence is retained through exact photon-sector
simulation resources. Their optimal separable comparisons and
asymptotic entanglement density produce a concave energy function that
bounds the entanglement increase at each use, including for arbitrary
correlated memories. The same function vanishes in the
entanglement-breaking region and recovers the corresponding PLOB
bound at infinite energy.

The finite-energy examples improve the evaluated upper-bound
benchmarks and leave an explicit gap to hashing. Closing this gap
requires further achievability results or a tighter converse.
The present claims concern vanishing-error energy-constrained
capacities. Public vacuum dilution under an unconditional mean-energy
constraint, analyzed in Ref.~\cite[Appendix F 1]{LossAmplifier},
prevents inferring an
energy-dependent strong converse merely from the weak-converse bound.
The exact strong-converse thresholds of the noisy channels are not
determined here. Finite-blocklength refinements and tighter photon-number
constraints provide further directions for the sector method.

